    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section class="hero">
        <div class="hero-container">
            <h1 class="hero-title">International Securities Identification Number (ISIN)</h1>
            <p class="hero-subtitle">Uganda Securities Exchange - National Numbering Agency for Uganda, recognized by ANNA</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <main class="main-content">
        <!-- About ISIN -->
        <section class="section">
            <h2 class="section-title">About ISIN at USE</h2>
            <div class="section-content">
                <p class="content-text">
                    The Uganda Securities Exchange is a member of the Association of National Numbering Agencies (ANNA) and is recognized by the latter as the <strong>National Numbering Agency for Uganda</strong>.
                </p>
                <p class="content-text">
                    Since 2010, the USE is responsible for codifying financial instruments issued by issuers that are registered in Uganda and financial instruments where the lead manager's registered office is in Uganda in accordance with the ISO-6166 Standard.
                </p>
                <p class="content-text">
                    The securities for which the USE allocates ISIN codes include those issued by global business companies registered in Uganda.
                </p>

                <div class="highlight-box">
                    <h3>Additional Codes Allocated by USE</h3>
                    <p>
                        The USE also allocates <strong>CFI Codes</strong> (Classification of financial instruments) and <strong>FISN</strong> (Financial Instrument Short Name) to securities in accordance with ISO-10962 and ISO-18774 respectively.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <p class="content-text">
                    The ISIN codes allocated to listed companies are shown on the contract notes, transaction reports as well as other reports provided by USE.
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- ANNA External Link -->
        <div class="external-link-box">
            <h3>Learn More About ANNA</h3>
            <a href="https://www.anna-web.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                <i class="fas fa-external-link-alt"></i>
                Visit ANNA Website
            </a>
        </div>

        <!-- Application Process -->
        <section class="section">
            <h2 class="section-title">How to Apply for an ISIN</h2>
            <div class="section-content">
                <div class="process-steps">
                    <div class="step">
                        <div class="step-number">1</div>
                        <div class="step-content">
                            <h3>File Application</h3>
                            <p>Applicants and/or representatives must file an application with Uganda Securities Exchange for an ISIN.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="step">
                        <div class="step-number">2</div>
                        <div class="step-content">
                            <h3>Provide Required Data</h3>
                            <p>The minimum set of data necessary for an ISIN allocation may depend on the requirements specified by the ISO 6166 Standard, ANNA Guidelines, the type of financial instrument involved and any other data prescribed by the USE, including, but not limited to, any supporting documentation.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="step">
                        <div class="step-number">3</div>
                        <div class="step-content">
                            <h3>Receive ISIN Code</h3>
                            <p>In accordance with ANNA guidelines, the USE will allocate ISINs in a timely manner, usually within 24 hours following the request or the next business day, provided the correct documentation is provided with the request.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Key Features Grid -->
        <div class="info-grid">
            <div class="info-card">
                <div class="info-card-icon">
                    <i class="fas fa-clock"></i>
                </div>
                <h3 class="info-card-title">Fast Turnaround</h3>
                <p class="info-card-text">
                    ISIN allocation typically completed within 24 hours or the next business day when all correct documentation is provided.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <div class="info-card-icon">
                    <i class="fas fa-certificate"></i>
                </div>
                <h3 class="info-card-title">ISO Compliance</h3>
                <p class="info-card-text">
                    All codes allocated in accordance with ISO-6166, ISO-10962, and ISO-18774 international standards.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <div class="info-card-icon">
                    <i class="fas fa-globe"></i>
                </div>
                <h3 class="info-card-title">ANNA Recognition</h3>
                <p class="info-card-text">
                    Officially recognized by the Association of National Numbering Agencies as Uganda's National Numbering Agency.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Download Section -->
        <div class="download-section">
            <h2 class="section-title">Download ISIN Codes</h2>
            <p class="content-text" style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">Access the complete list of ISIN, CFI and FISN codes for securities listed on the Uganda Securities Exchange.</p>
            <a href="#" class="download-btn">
                <i class="fas fa-download"></i>
                Download List of ISIN, CFI and FISN Codes
            </a>
        </div>
